        <p>Do not submit confidential business information, trade secrets, privileged material, copyrighted material you lack permission to use, or highly sensitive personal information. Submitting an idea, design, proposed service, or in-kind offer does not obligate us to keep it confidential, compensate you, accept it, or refrain from using similar ideas independently, except as stated in a separate signed agreement.</p>
        <h2>5. Donations, Pledges, and Gifts</h2>
        <p>Gifts promoted through this site are made to the Foundation, a IRC § 501(c)(3) charitable organization (EIN 20-2960627), designated for North Kitsap United. Tax deductibility and substantiation depend on individual facts and law. Donors should consult their own tax, legal, and financial advisers. No statement on this site is a guarantee of deductibility, valuation, tax treatment, project completion, or use beyond the Foundation’s legally enforceable acceptance of an approved restriction.</p>
        <p>The Foundation may accept, decline, condition, return, redirect with donor consent, or seek modification of a proposed gift to the extent permitted by law and its gift-acceptance policies. A pledge or proposed gift is not accepted merely because a form is submitted. Gifts involving securities, real estate, closely held interests, tangible property, retirement assets, donor-advised funds, matching gifts, restrictions, naming, sponsorship, or in-kind value may require additional review, documentation, valuation, custody, environmental review, title review, or professional advice.</p>
        <p>Donor-advised fund grants and qualified charitable distributions may be subject to restrictions on benefits, pledges, sponsorships, tickets, goods, services, and enforceable commitments. Donors should coordinate with their sponsoring organization, IRA custodian, and advisers before submission.</p>
        <h2>6. Payment Processing, Receipts, Errors, Refunds, and Reversals</h2>
        <p>Card and bank-transfer gifts are completed on Foundation donation pages hosted by Zeffy and processed through Stripe, and are subject to those providers’ terms. An optional contribution displayed by Zeffy supports Zeffy, not North Kitsap United, and may be adjustable by the donor. Third-party fees, holds, verification, chargebacks, reversals, outages, errors, fraud controls, and processing times are outside our complete control.</p>
        <p>The Foundation will issue acknowledgments or receipts as it determines appropriate under applicable law. A receipt is not tax advice and may be corrected. Unless required by law or approved by the Foundation under a written policy, completed charitable gifts are generally final and nonrefundable. Requests involving duplicate transactions, processing errors, unauthorized activity, failed conditions, or other extraordinary circumstances must be submitted promptly and will be reviewed individually. Any approved refund may be returned to the original payment source, reduced by unrecoverable third-party charges where lawful, and may require correction of acknowledgments and records.</p>
